---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
---

<InfoLayout
  title="Licences and attribution: Herden"
  description="Herden licence and upstream software attribution."
  eyebrow="Licence record"
  heading="Licences + attribution"
  canonicalPath="/licenses"
>
  <p>
    Herden is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Every Host
    installation includes the full licence and attribution notice under
    <code>~/.local/share/doc/herden</code>.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p><strong>Current Host release: 0.9.8</strong></p>
    <p>
      <a href="/releases/host-v0.9.8/LICENSE">Apache-2.0 licence</a> ·
      <a href="/releases/host-v0.9.8/NOTICE">Release notice</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Upstream work</h2>
  <p>
    Herden includes and modifies software from the Apache-2.0 projects
    <a href="https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr">herdr</a> and
    <a href="https://github.com/ZingerLittleBee/Heeler">Heeler</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The native iOS application, plugin, relay, and original landing site began
    from Heeler, including the iOS QR scanner, secure pairing flow, and file
    upload foundation. The Host runtime began from herdr. Herden’s work includes
    product integration, moving inherited Host-side pairing into Rust, compact
    Pairing Codes, Space-first navigation, shared terminal controls, and the iOS
    Share Extension.
  </p>
  <p>
    Neither upstream project endorses Herden. Their names are used only to
    describe the origin of the software.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party components</h2>
  <p>
    The iOS app uses pinned builds of libssh2, OpenSSL, and libghostty-spm.
    Their required notices ship with the corresponding application or release
    bundle. The website uses JetBrains Mono under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
